<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ashir</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Achir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ashir was a fortified town in the Titteri mountains of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, founded around 936 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanhaja">Sanhaja</a> chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziri-ibn-manad">Ziri ibn Manad</a> with the approval of the Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>. It was the first seat of the Zirid family, who served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> from there, and remained a regional centre after the Zirids moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> in 972. Its ruins lie in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medea">Médéa</a> province.</p></div>
